92	    // case, so it is truncated like any other over-cap step rather than reported as
93	    // a failure — and the buffer is set above the cap precisely so this branch means
94	    // "far too much", never "slightly over". Decided FIRST, because overrunning the
95	    // buffer also kills the child, which would otherwise read as a timeout.
